# Close an issue with Fixes #N

When a change closes a GitHub issue, write `Fixes #N` in both places:

- The changelog bullet for that change.
- The body of the pull request that merges into `master`.

Use the plain text `Fixes #125`. A changelog link such as `[#125](https://github.com/ctucker1984/remember/issues/125)` does not close the issue. GitHub closes it when that pull request merges.

Leave `Fixes` off an issue this change does not close.

```markdown
- **Fix:** An admission ticket prints the member's legal first and last name. Fixes #125
```
